  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Y-Med Blue Economy: Facilitating Skills Circulation between Libya and Italy in the Fisheries Sector</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">knowledge transfer and increased collaboration in this area of work across the two sides of the Mediterranean. The project comprises a preparatory phase in Libya, a 6-month internship in Italy and a placement phase in Libya upon completion of the internship. This project will be part of the broader Y-med initiative, a circular migration scheme run by IOM in Italy to support youth from Mediterranean countries (Egypt, Libya, Tunisia and Morocco) with skills development and knowledge transfer through 6-month internships in Italian companies. In its first three editions, Y-med involved a total of 78 interns from the above-mentioned North African countries and 41 Italian companies based in two Italian regions (Veneto and Lazio).Thanks to  the Y-med Blue Economy project, IOM will have the chance to enrich the Y-med initiative, expanding its regional collaborations in Italy (involving companies from Friuli Venezia Giulia Region) and targeting specifically the blue economy (a key sector for Mediterranean economies).</narrative>
  </description>
